# Cursor Rules for Arise

You are working on `arise`, a modular Git worktree and Herdr workspace orchestrator.

## Core Rules & Invariants
1. Read `AGENTS.md` and `types.d.ts` before modifying code.
2. Keep the core engine in `lib/` 100% workplace- and repo-agnostic. Never hardcode workspace paths in `lib/`.
3. Keep layouts declarative using `lib/layout.js`.
4. Never delete protected branches or the repository root.

## Documentation & Type Synchronization Rule (CRITICAL)
Whenever you make any change to the codebase:
1. Update `types.d.ts` if any interfaces, flags, or configuration shapes changed.
2. Update relevant files in `docs/` (`docs/architecture.md`, `docs/preset-guide.md`, `docs/config-reference.md`) and `README.md`.
3. Update `arise.schema.json` and `worktree.schema.json` if config options were added/modified.
4. Run `npm test` and verify that all unit tests (including `test/docs-sync.test.js`) pass 100%.
